\subsection{Robustness under deployment stress: imbalance and federation}

\rev{The two stressors closer to deployment changed the comparison in different ways:
class imbalance moved the hand-crafted features ahead of ECGFounder, and non-IID
federation brought the means of the two closer while their spread over site draws
differed. Under class imbalance, at the natural-like 9:1 SR:AF ratio (majority 0.90),
every representation's ARI fell. These results used power scaling and [GAP: the clusterer
of the 9:1 results, which the manuscript does not name], over the ten seeds. The
hand-crafted features retained the most structure (ARI 0.265 [0.250, 0.280], AMI 0.245
[0.233, 0.257]) and \emph{overtook} ECGFounder (ARI 0.063 [0.061, 0.065], AMI 0.148
[0.143, 0.152]), with no overlap between the two ARI intervals. HuBERT-ECG reached the
same ARI as ECGFounder (0.061 [0.053, 0.069]) at a lower AMI (0.044 [0.037, 0.050]). At
this ratio its partition therefore agreed with the classes on record pairs as often as
ECGFounder's but shared less information with them. The raw and conv-AE pipelines stayed
at chance (0.000 and 0.004). The reversal holds for this ratio, scaler and clusterer, the
only imbalanced setting evaluated.}

\rev{Under non-IID federation the three representations that cluster above chance lost
unequal shares of their centralized ARI (Table~\ref{tab:fed} and Fig.~\ref{fig:fed}).
ECGFounder fell from 0.885 to 0.612, the hand-crafted features from 0.644 to 0.591 and
HuBERT-ECG from 0.174 to 0.106, while raw flattening stayed at 0.000 in every setting.
Under IID federation across ten sites every representation retained essentially its
centralized ARI, which validates the federated procedure. The hand-crafted features
retained 92\% of their centralized ARI, the largest share. ECGFounder's lead over them
narrowed accordingly, from 0.885 against 0.644 centralized to 0.612 against 0.591 under
non-IID federation. The two means were close, and they did not carry the same risk. Across
the ten redrawn site partitions the hand-crafted bootstrap interval was [0.546, 0.631] and
the worst single partition still returned 0.455, whereas ECGFounder's interval was
[0.382, 0.796] and three of its ten partitions fell to 0.132 or below, one of them to
chance. We judge a deployment by the worst site draw as well as by the average one,
because each real site has one class mix, which may be an unfavourable one. On that
criterion the 16 hand-crafted features were the more predictable of the two under site
heterogeneity.}

